## Why This Is Asked
Cross-brand data collaboration is a real-world need for regulated industries, demanding privacy-preserving analytics, governance, and robust DR. This question probes Azure-native design choices that balance data utility with compliance.

## Key Concepts
- Data clean room architectures and governance
- Privacy-preserving analytics (differential privacy, secure enclaves)
- Data contracts and consent management
- BYOK with Key Vault and Purview lineage
- Cross-region DR and data residency considerations

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: enforce privacy contract before sharing results
function enforceContract(dataset) {
  const nonPII = dropPII(dataset);
  const privatized = applyDifferentialPrivacy(nonPII, {epsilon: 1.0});
  return privatized;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you prove compliance to regulators and auditors?
- How would you handle evolving data contracts and versioning?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end Azure-native, multi-tenant data platform design under regulatory constraints with real-time processing, governance, security, disaster recovery, and cost discipline.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-tenant isolation and per-tenant policy enforcement
- EU data residency with bring-your-own-key (BYOK) encryption
- Real-time event processing using Durable Functions
- Data governance with Purview and token-based sharing mechanisms
- Disaster recovery to paired region with automated failover strategies
- Cost optimization through serverless analytics, auto-scaling, and resource quotas

## Code Example
```javascript
// Durable Function snippet: policy check and redaction (pseudo-code)
module.exports = async function (context, req) {
  const tenantId = req.headers['x-tenant-id'];
  const eventData = req.body;

  // Per-tenant policy validation
  const policy = await getTenantPolicy(tenantId);
  if (!validateEvent(eventData, policy)) {
    context.res = { status: 403, body: 'Policy violation' };
    return;
  }

  // PII redaction
  const redactedData = redactPII(eventData, policy.piiRules);

  // Store to ADLS and trigger downstream processing
  await storeToADLS(tenantId, redactedData);
  await triggerSynapseProcessing(tenantId, redactedData);
};
```
